var englishChannelThemes = map[string]theme{
	"1-8":   {"Creative contribution", "Creative expression meets the sharing of an individual contribution. Consider both making an original piece of work and finding a suitable context in which to share it.", "Describe what makes your contribution individual and choose a setting for it.", "Where does my way of expressing myself find a response?"},
	"2-14":  {"Direction and resources", "Finding a direction meets the allocation of resources. The meaning of a goal and where your effort goes can be considered together.", "List the time, skills and support available for one goal.", "Do my resources support the direction I chose?"},
	"3-60":  {"Change and a new order", "A new order taking shape meets the limits of current circumstances. A change may begin in an unsettled way and develop in stages; continuous innovation is not a requirement.", "Develop a change through small experiments and name its limits.", "Which condition needs to develop before this change can proceed?"},
	"4-63":  {"Questions and logical explanations", "Questioning meets the formation of an answer. Use this theme to frame a hypothesis clearly and test it against evidence.", "Write a question, a possible answer and a way to test it separately.", "How has this answer been tested?"},
	"5-15":  {"Rhythm and different tempos", "Personal routines meet room for different rhythms of life. Differences in pace within a shared arrangement can become a useful observation.", "Describe your rhythm without treating someone else's pace as a standard.", "Can different rhythms coexist in this arrangement?"},
	"6-59":  {"Closeness and boundaries", "Closeness meets emotional boundaries. Observe the quality of an intimate relationship through mutual openness, consent and timing; this is not a prediction of fertility or a relationship's future.", "Discuss closeness alongside each person's need for space.", "Are both people's boundaries visible?"},
	"7-31":  {"Shared direction and leadership", "A group's direction meets guidance that is heard. Consider the connection between a proposal, participation and the shared goal rather than relying on a leadership title.", "Clarify the group's contribution and decision areas around a proposed direction.", "Whose participation shapes this direction?"},
	"9-52":  {"Focus and stillness", "Attention to detail meets the ability to pause. Creating suitable conditions for concentration becomes a practical theme to observe.", "Reduce distractions and choose one completion criterion.", "What conditions help me concentrate?"},
	"10-20": {"Aligned expression in the moment", "Behavior aligned with yourself meets present expression. Observe how your words connect with your values in a particular situation.", "Write an action that supports something you said.", "Do my words and actions point in the same direction?"},
	"10-34": {"Acting in your own direction", "Individual behavior meets practical power. Observe how you relate your effort to chosen activities rather than only to outside expectations.", "Describe the connection between an effort and your own values.", "Is my own direction present in what I am doing?"},
	"10-57": {"Behavior and immediate awareness", "Your behavior meets awareness of the current situation. Explore how a first impression influences your response in a specific encounter.", "Record an initial observation alongside the behavior that followed.", "How did I respond to the signal I noticed?"},
	"11-56": {"Ideas and stories", "Ideas meet the sharing of experience through a story. Distinguish an account that offers a perspective from evidence that establishes a conclusion.", "Share an idea through an example and explain the example's limits.", "Which perspective does this story offer the listener?"},
	"12-22": {"Feeling and timely expression", "Social openness meets the timing of expression. Observe how emotional experience enters a conversation. This channel defines the Solar Plexus; refer to the emotional authority section for decisions.", "Consider your readiness and the listener's space before an important conversation.", "Under which conditions can I express this clearly?"},
	"13-33": {"Listening and sharing experience", "Witnessing meets retreat and reflection. Consider how an experience can be held, understood and shared at a suitable time.", "Separate your own story from another person's private information.", "Do I have a suitable time and permission to share this story?"},
	"16-48": {"Depth and skill", "Deep understanding meets skills developed through practice. Compare a feeling of competence with concrete work and feedback.", "Create a small cycle of practice and feedback for one skill.", "How well can I apply what I know?"},
	"17-62": {"Explaining a view through details", "A framework meets detailed expression. Consider the consistency of an explanation, its evidence and the listener's needs together.", "Explain a view through one main claim and three supporting points.", "Do these details make my view understandable?"},
	"18-58": {"The wish to improve", "Recognizing what could be corrected meets enthusiasm for improvement. Timing, requested feedback and a practical suggestion can make a difference.", "Name what works alongside one improvement to a process.", "Does my wish to correct something provide a concrete benefit?"},
	"19-49": {"Needs and principles", "Sensitivity to needs meets conditions of acceptance. Consider whose needs are seen in a group and which agreements shape the arrangement.", "Discuss the need, the principle and each person's expectations.", "Do the principles of this arrangement actually meet its needs?"},
	"20-34": {"Present application", "Expression in the present meets practical power. Distinguish being busy from making a chosen contribution; this channel does not require fast decisions.", "Name the purpose of a task and use your authority section when deciding.", "Does what I am doing serve a purpose I chose?"},
	"20-57": {"Expressing immediate awareness", "A subtle observation meets expression in the moment. Consider the context and the listener's space before stating an initial impression.", "Describe a signal as an observation rather than a definitive judgment.", "Is what I am saying an observation or an interpretation?"},
	"21-45": {"Managing shared resources", "Responsibility for resources meets their distribution in a group. Consider authority, contribution and transparency together; no financial outcome is predicted.", "Write the decision and distribution rules for a shared resource.", "Are responsibilities and expectations around management clear?"},
	"23-43": {"Making an insight understandable", "An individual insight meets a simple explanation. Consider when and how to share an idea as well as what makes it new.", "Share an insight through a concrete example and a short explanation.", "Which context does the listener need?"},
	"24-61": {"Reconsidering an inner question", "An inner question meets returning to a thought. Distinguish curiosity that creates understanding from being caught in the same question.", "Pause a thought that adds no new information and name what remains unanswered.", "What has this thinking process added?"},
	"25-51": {"Stepping beyond the familiar", "Open-heartedness meets testing yourself. Observe what changes in a new experience without treating the channel as a prediction of unexpected events.", "Clarify the purpose and actual conditions of an experiment.", "What do I want to explore in this step?"},
	"26-44": {"Patterns and effective presentation", "Recognizing past patterns meets persuasion. When sharing what experience taught you, consider accuracy and the limits of what you promise.", "Describe the experience behind a proposal and what is different today.", "Does my promise match my actual capacity?"},
	"27-50": {"Care and responsibility", "Support meets protective values. Observe who receives care, its scope and the capacity available to provide it.", "Discuss boundaries and other responsibilities within a support arrangement.", "Is the responsibility for care shared fairly?"},
	"28-38": {"Standing for something meaningful", "Meaning in an effort meets defending a value. Consider what purpose each struggle or objection serves.", "Write the value of an effort alongside its continuing cost.", "Why does this effort matter to me?"},
	"29-46": {"Discovery through participation", "Saying yes to an experience meets being present in it. Consider your participation conditions and what you learn without needing to control the outcome.", "Clarify the scope and your capacity before joining an experience.", "Can I actually sustain this yes?"},
	"30-41": {"Imagination and desire for experience", "Imagining a possibility meets wanting an experience. Keep expectations distinct from the experience that actually unfolds.", "Consider different possible outcomes alongside the one you imagine.", "Would I still want the experience if the outcome changed?"},
	"32-54": {"Development and continuity", "The wish to progress meets recognizing what can last. Consider development alongside the values you preserve and the conditions you face.", "Identify what you want to preserve within a change.", "Which value do I want to sustain while things develop?"},
	"34-57": {"Power and subtle awareness", "Practical power meets awareness of immediate signals. Observe how effort and awareness work together in a task; this is not a health or safety assessment.", "Record what you noticed during a task and how you responded.", "Am I noticing the situation while directing my effort?"},
	"35-36": {"Learning through new experience", "A desire for change meets learning in an unfamiliar situation. Make room to process an intense experience before treating it as a general rule.", "Compare what you expected with what the experience taught you.", "What did this experience actually teach me?"},
	"37-40": {"Agreement and reciprocity", "Support in close relationships meets effort and rest. Turn implicit expectations into clear agreements where possible.", "Discuss the exchange, effort and personal time involved in a shared task.", "Does this agreement make room for both contribution and rest?"},
	"39-55": {"Bringing emotional meaning into view", "Emotional movement meets the meaning of an experience. Observe how feelings change in an encounter without assuming that someone must be provoked.", "Open a difficult emotional topic at a suitable time and with mutual willingness.", "Which feeling or need became visible in this encounter?"},
	"42-53": {"Beginning and completing a cycle", "Beginning a process meets bringing it to completion. Consider the stage of a task and the conditions that define its completion.", "Write the starting, developing and completion criteria for a project.", "Which stage is this process in?"},
	"47-64": {"From impressions to understanding", "Scattered impressions meet making sense of experience. Observe connections that emerge over time without forcing the past into one explanation.", "Record the parts of an event without interpretation, then revisit them.", "How has new information changed my understanding?"},
}
